[claude-setup] SDK 0209, synced to the project folder in setup tool 2.27.0 (2026-11-03, folder only; owner ~08:05
"Please sync the folder with stuff that works", answer "Add tested extras, folder only"). claude-9b-think's draft 0209
(c9b-think/owner-1102/0209-system-link-copies-on-one-pc.UNTESTED.patch, md5 b2abfa34) and its r1
(0209-r1-system-link-trace-and-xuid.UNTESTED.diff, eec26ded) folded into one diff. The three files come out byte for
byte as in claude-9b-test's tested tree ob29d before 0210 (xam_net.cpp ffcdbdd0, xgi_app.cpp 7a3ddc43,
user_profile.cpp 74f9e7a1).
What it does: system link between copies of cod3mp on one PC. A loopback net_interface (127.0.0.N) is that copy's
system link address; binds to "any address" go to it; an unbound datagram socket is bound to it before its first send;
broadcasts also go as unicast to each net_broadcast_peers address (new, Net, default empty), and with a loopback address
the real broadcast is skipped. net_trace (Net, default off) logs the network calls and datagrams. With a loopback
net_interface the XUID's low 32 bits are that address (one XUID per copy); LAN addresses keep the old XUID.
XSessionLeaveLocal/Remote (0xB0013) answered; session create/join/leave/delete logged. Real LANs are unchanged unless
net_broadcast_peers is set.
Tested with 0210: claude-9b-test q-22 (ob29d, 2026-11-03 04:45: host and joiner both PASSED on mp_merv) and
claude-setup's sync1103 build and runs (dev/agents/claude-setup/SYNC-2026-11-03.md). The "UNTESTED" marks in the code
comments are from the drafts.

